      en: "Amerongse Berg is the highest point in the Dutch province of Utrecht at 67 meters. It lies within the Utrechtse Heuvelrug National Park, an ice-age moraine landscape. The hill formed during the Saale glaciation about 150,000 years ago as glaciers pushed sand and gravel. The summit is forested with oak and beech. It offers panoramic views over the Rhine valley. Amerongse Berg is a popular hiking destination; several marked trails lead to the top. The area hosts roe deer, wild boar, and red deer. Average annual precipitation is around 850 mm.",
