      en: "Duin- en Kruidberg is an estate and nature reserve in the province of North Holland, Netherlands, located in the dunes near Santpoort. The area covers about 600 hectares and consists of dunes, forests, and meadows. It is part of Zuid-Kennemerland National Park. The Duin- en Kruidberg mansion was built in 1878 in neo-Gothic style and served as a summer residence. Today it houses a hotel and restaurant. The nature reserve is known for its biodiversity, including fallow deer, foxes, and various bird species. Hikers and cyclists can explore the area on a network of trails. Dunes reach heights of up to 50 meters.",
